think Lindy-first, crux-first among the three siblings the distance_morph log named: a region-size/bounding-box reader over a LabelMap, a disk-element builder, a watershed. All roughly equal Lindy (durable image primitives). Crux-first takes the hardest-solvable that opens the rest -- the REGION reader, the natural consumer of the labeler: it turns segmentation into measurement, and a blob filter, a size histogram, and a character isolator all descend from being able to measure a labeled region. A watershed is larger and less cleanly tractable in one lap; the disk-element builder is a smaller supporting piece.
