think Designed image/regions.rye as one coherent SLC over three tightly-composed verbs: measure_regions (one raster pass, one Region per dense label -- area plus running min/max bbox), filter_min_area (the despeckle -- drop components below a threshold, recompact survivors to dense 1..count in raster order), render_mask (close the loop -- labeling back to a binary white-on-black mask read through branch.is_on). Compose not braid: owns only accumulation, remap, binary render; label owns the LabelMap, branch.is_on the binary door, qoi the buffer. No new gather/blend/codec/color.
think Chose the fixtures crux-first: an L of three 8-connected pixels is the decisive bounding-box fixture -- its 2x2 box (four cells) is provably larger than its three-pixel area, so a box is a different fact from a count. A lone speck (area 1) with a clear gap is the despeckle target. Same scene proves area, raster order, bbox, despeckle, and render-mask.
obs GREEN on the FIRST metal run, no algorithm reds. TAME caught one compound assert (`assert(l >= 1 and l <= map.count)`) -- split into two named asserts so the failing half names itself, re-GREEN. width-check exit 0, ASCII clean, living_docs_lint GREEN, living_card_ascii_witness GREEN.
obs Dense-labeling invariant is load-bearing: because label.rye compacts to a gap-free 1..count, every Region meets at least one pixel, so `area == 0` safely marks an untouched region for the first-pixel box seed, and the postcondition `area >= 1` holds for all.
